```md
# Online Shop + Inventory System (Beginner Friendly)

This project is a simple online shop connected to an inventory system.

✅ Customers can buy items (stock goes down)  
✅ You can restock items (stock goes up)  
✅ Low-stock items (stock < 5) are shown and backend prints a LOW STOCK log  
✅ Stock change history is saved in the database

---

## What you need to install

### Option A (Easiest): Docker Desktop
Install Docker Desktop:
- Windows / Mac: Docker Desktop

After installing, restart your computer if needed.

### Option B (Advanced): Node.js + PostgreSQL manually
Not recommended if you're not comfortable coding.

---

## How to start (Docker method)

### 1) Download / create the project folder
Make sure you have this structure:

online-shop-inventory/
  docker-compose.yml
  README.md
  backend/
  frontend/

### 2) Start everything
Open a terminal in the project folder and run:

```bash
docker compose up
```

The first run can take a few minutes because it downloads images and installs packages.

### 3) Open the website
- Shop page (buy items): http://localhost:5173
- Backend API health check: http://localhost:3001/health

---

## How to stop
In the terminal where Docker is running, press:

CTRL + C

Then run:

```bash
docker compose down
```

---

## Database tables (created automatically)

When Docker starts the database for the first time, it automatically runs:

- backend/sql/001_init.sql  (creates tables)
- backend/sql/002_seed.sql  (adds example products)

Tables:
- products (id, sku, name, price_cents, stock, updated_at)
- stock_history (audit log of stock changes)

---

## What to click in the app

### Shop tab
- Click "Buy 1" to purchase a product.
- If stock is 0, you cannot buy.
- If stock becomes low, it will show as low.

### Dashboard tab
- View all current inventory.
- See low-stock items.
- Click "Restock +5" to add stock.

---

## API endpoints (for reference)

Backend base URL: http://localhost:3001

- GET  /api/products
- GET  /api/low-stock
- POST /api/purchase   body: { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 }
- POST /api/restock    body: { "productId": 1, "quantity": 5 }
- GET  /api/history/:productId

---

## Troubleshooting

### "Port already in use"
Something else is using ports 5173, 3001, or 5432.

Fix:
- Close the other app, or
- Change ports in docker-compose.yml

### "Database is empty"
If you already started before and want fresh data:

⚠️ This will delete your database data.

```bash
docker compose down -v
docker compose up
```

---

## Notes
This is a simple demo system.
In real businesses, you would add:
- user login
- payment gateway
- admin authentication for restock
- better product images, etc.
